 Truesdale\nLicensed Veterinary Technician\nSky Buzzell\nDr. Pamela White\nVeterinary Radiation Oncologist\nDr. Angharad Waite\nVeterinary Medical Oncologist\nDr. Shannon Kenny\nVeterinary Medical Oncologist\nDr. Christina Manley\nVeterinary Medical Oncologist\nDr. Rick Chetney, Jr.\nRadiation Oncologist\nAna Galarza\nVeterinary Assistant\nDr. Tony Rusk\nAssociate Veterinarian (Oncology)\nRobyn Dickey\nVeterinary Technician\nKaitlyn Mrkal\nVeterinary Technician\nSeth Swint\nVeterinary Assistant\nStephanie Gutgesell\nVeterinary Technician\nKarla Alfaro\nClient Care Specialist\nHannah Dellinger\nVeterinary Assistant\nMaggie Lanaghan\nVeterinary Assistant\nDeirdre Hilden\nClient Care Specialist\nCandace Johnson\nLicensed Veterinary Technician\nTheresa House\nLicensed Veterinary Technician\nKimberly Kelsey\nLicensed Veterinary Technician\nTeressa Baker\nLicensed Veterinary Technician\nKatie Cummings\nVeterinary Assistant\nAlly Cox\nVeterinary Assistant\nNicki Butler\nVeterinary Assistant\nHeather Deshazo\nClient Care Specialist\nSpencer Thompson\nClient Care Specialist\nJen Fenton\nReferral Coordinator\nDr. Heather Wilson-Robles\nVeterinary Medical Oncologist\nDr. Kathleen Tidd\nVeterinary Medical Oncologist\nDr. Cassandra Rodenbaugh\nVeterinary Oncologist\nSee More\nAbout The Oncology Service\nOur highly-educated and friendly team will be with you every step of the way to ensure your pet's comfort and health are front and center. We love what we do, and like you, we want nothing more than to help your companion live a longer, healthier and happier life. There is no better team to provide you the support and confidence you need to make the decisions that are right for you and your family.\nLearn More\nThey Love Us\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\nThis has been a stressful time for us and everyone in this office has been fabulous and made this experience much better. They are warm, welcoming, and compassionate! The entire office has been fabulous but Angela has been very compassionate and willing to help with Finley.\nKatie G.\nI honestly can't think of a thing you could have done better. I'm very impressed with the entire practice. From the moment we walked in, it was smooth sailing! Both myself and Khylo were greeted by name and escorted to a very comfortable and bright room.\nJanet L.\nSee More\nBlogs\nRecent Updates\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\n23 Amazing Facts About Dogs You Probably Didn't Know\nDo you think you know everything there is to know ...\nSee More\nWhat to Do When You Are Traveling During Your Pet’s Chemotherapy Protocol\nWhether you are traveling for business or pleasure...\nSee More\nHow to Spot an Ear Infection In Your Dog\nDid you know that some dogs are more prone to ear ...\nSee More\n8 Signs of Separation Anxiety in Cats And What to Do About Them\nWe’ve all seen the memes since this\nSee More\nSee More\nExpanded Services Menu\nMedical Oncology\nRadiation Oncology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nStereotactic Radiation Therapy\nElectrochemotherapy\nOutpatient Imaging\nVisit our office to get the latest in top-quality veterinary care along with unparalleled service\nLinks\nAbout Us\nServices\nResources\nContact Us\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nLogin / Account\nGet In Touch\nTOS - Leesburg\n(571) 209-1176\nleesburg@tosvets.com\nTOS - Richmond\n(804) 999-0001\nrichmond@tosvets.com\nTOS - Springfield\n(703) 451-8900, option 2\nspringfield@tosvets.com\nHow Are We Doing?\nReview Us\nfacebook\ninstagram\nX\nThe Oncology Service - Springfield\nThe Oncology Service - Richmond\nThe Oncology Service - Leesburg\n©2025 The Oncology Service. Resource Articles ©2025 KARMAjack. All Rights Reserved.\nVeterinary websites by KARMAjack\nNotice\nTemporary Closure Notice\nOur hospital will be closed from\nSeptember 8–12\nfor unexpected facility repairs.\nWe’re working quickly to get everything resolved. In the meantime, our team will be monitoring our email and voicemail remotely.\nThank you for your patience and understanding, we can’t wait to